# ListenBrainz: the sources ExportSources lifts to the meta level.
#
# Three parts, three publishers' shapes. The MusicBrainz identifier joins them and is declared
# nowhere between the three dumps.

# Popularity aggregates, published as CSV.
postgres     pg     listenbrainz  top_recording
postgres     pg     listenbrainz  mlhd_top_recording

# The listen events. Nested three levels deep, with an artist-identifier array, and with contents
# that vary per record because what a submitting client reports is up to the client. This is where
# the array and nested-path scopes come from.
mongo        mongo  listenbrainz  listens

# The artist cache, one entity per artist, carrying a Wikidata URL among its relationships. No
# edges: the dump relates artists to other sites rather than to each other.
neo4j-label  graph  neo4j         LBArtist
